# Nisc Cloud website workflow

Re-read `NISC-CLOUD-WEBSITE-STRATEGY.md` before website work. Originals live in `Reference artwork/` at the repo root. Adapted assets go in `apps/www.nisccloud.com/public/artwork/`. There is a separate `Reference artwork s/` copy; do not edit it unless asked.

## Artwork

- Use the supplied reference as the primary visual source. Keep its composition, people, layout and design elements unless the owner asks for a change.
- Replace embedded wording with accurate Nisc service copy. Do not invent results, SLAs, prices or partner tiers.
- Adjust colour only where needed to fit Nisc sky blue, midnight `#02070A` and restrained orange `#FC734D`.
- When creating or replacing people, depict Black African/Kenyan people. Leave people already in an approved reference as they are.
- Never overwrite a reference file. Save the adaptation under a new name.
- Edit vectors when they exist (`Picture2.svg`, `Picture3.svg`, and cleaned SVGs already in `public/artwork/`). If the source is a flattened PNG, JPG or WebP, name the image-editing tool required before promising exact text replacement.

## Motion and services

Give each service its own visual story and animation. Do not reuse the same cursor, dashboard or progress bar across services. Static photos must not run animation timers. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Implementation

- Use Bun (`bun`, `bun run`). Do not discard, reset or stash existing uncommitted work.
- In the browser, check desktop, mobile, dark mode and reduced motion on every changed route before calling the work done.
- After a meaningful change, append the strategy change log: date, files/routes, reason, evidence, validation, outcome and what is still open. Do not mark planned work complete.
